    ;;
    remove|rm) cat <<'EOF'
perch remove — unregister a project. Does not stop it or touch its files.

USAGE
  perch remove <name>       (alias: perch rm <name>)
EOF
    ;;
    list|ls) cat <<'EOF'
perch list — show every registered project and whether its port is currently up.

USAGE
  perch list                (alias: perch ls)
EOF
    ;;
    autoplace|auto) cat <<'EOF'
perch autoplace — keep terminals arranged automatically (via yabai signals).

USAGE
  perch autoplace           show status (default)
  perch autoplace on        install signals: every new Terminal window or display change
                            re-runs `perch place empty` (debounced). Persisted to ~/.yabairc.
  perch autoplace off       remove the signals + clean ~/.yabairc
  perch autoplace now       run `perch place empty` once, right now

Needs yabai. `on` makes it survive a yabai restart; `off` fully disables it.
EOF
    ;;
    groups|clusters|cluster|by-product) cat <<'EOF'
perch groups — list projects grouped by product cluster (auto-grouped by name prefix).

USAGE
  perch groups              (aliases: perch clusters, perch cluster)

Projects are grouped by the part of the name before the first "-" (example-web -> example).
Each multi-project cluster shows how to start it all at once.

RELATED — start a whole cluster:
  perch example             start every example-* project (backend first)
  perch 'example*'          same (quote the * so the shell doesn't expand it)
