    ;;
    stop) cat <<'EOF'
perch stop — free a project's port (kill whatever is listening on it).

USAGE
  perch stop <project|port>
  perch stop all            alias for `perch killall`

Examples
  perch stop example-web
  perch stop 3001
EOF
    ;;
    clear|cls) cat <<'EOF'
perch clear — clear the text and scrollback of EVERY Terminal tab (like Cmd+K).

USAGE
  perch clear               (alias: perch cls)

Wipes each tab's display without stopping anything — servers keep running. Works
even in tabs running a live process (writes the clear escape straight to the tty,
which a plain `clear` can't do while a server holds the shell).
EOF
    ;;
    killall|kill-all|stopall) cat <<'EOF'
perch killall — stop running registered servers by freeing their ports.

USAGE
  perch killall             stop every running registered server
  perch killall fav         stop only the servers in your favorites
  perch killall --close     also close their Terminal tabs
EOF
    ;;
    set|settings) cat <<'EOF'
perch set — view or change optional behavior.

USAGE
  perch set                       show current settings
  perch set placement <on|off>    yabai desktop placement on launch/place (default on)
  perch set tile <on|off>         full-width stacked tiling during place (default on)
EOF
    ;;
    gui|dashboard|ui) cat <<'EOF'
perch gui — open the web dashboard.

USAGE
  perch gui                 open http://localhost:7620
  perch gui stop            stop the dashboard server
EOF
    ;;
    setup) cat <<'EOF'
perch setup — auto-detect this machine's monitors and write the desktop map (spaces.conf).

USAGE
  perch setup
EOF
    ;;
    doctor|check) cat <<'EOF'
perch doctor — check dependencies (osascript, python3, yabai) and configuration.

USAGE
  perch doctor              (alias: perch check)
EOF
    ;;
    bounds|pos|position) cat <<'EOF'
perch bounds — manage remembered free-floating window positions.

USAGE
  perch bounds              list remembered positions
  perch bounds clear        forget all positions
  perch bounds clear <name> forget one project's position
EOF
    ;;
    config) cat <<'EOF'
perch config — print the path to the projects registry file.

USAGE
  perch config              prints ~/.config/perch/projects.conf
EOF
    ;;
    port) cat <<'EOF'
perch port — print the perch-assigned port for a project.

USAGE
  perch port                the port for the project in the current directory
  perch port <name>         the port for a named registered project

Meant for use inside a project's own start script so it binds perch's port when
perch is installed, and the framework default otherwise:
  next dev  -p   $(perch port 2>/dev/null || echo 3000)
  vite --port    $(perch port 2>/dev/null || echo 5173) --strictPort
  react-native start --port $(perch port 2>/dev/null || echo 8081)
  PORT=$(perch port 2>/dev/null || echo 3000) nest start --watch
